  "decision_conditions": [
    "<div>The roof design of the proposed development is not considered respectful to the original dwelling and the terrace, therefore resulting in unacceptable impact on the character of the area. The proposed development would also remove the only window of the existing study room on the first floor, which is considered as a habitable room. It would completely block natural light and air permeating through to the room, which would result in inadequate living conditions to the residents. As such, the proposed development is contrary to:<br></div><div><br></div><div><p><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: \" pt=\"\" sans\",=\"\" sans-serif;\"=\"\">-\r\nNational Planning Policy Framework</span>&nbsp;(NPPF) (MHCLG, 2024)<o:p></o:p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: \" pt=\"\" sans\",=\"\" sans-serif;\"=\"\">- Policy D4 of the\r\nLondon Plan (March 2021)<o:p></o:p></span></p><p><span pt=\"\" sans\",=\"\" sans-serif;\"=\"\" style=\"font-size: 10.5pt;\">- Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD5 of t</span>he London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024); and</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: \" pt=\"\" sans\",=\"\" sans-serif;\"=\"\">- T</span>he London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s<span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt;\">&nbsp;Residential\r\nExtensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012).</span></p></div>"
  ],
